WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.260
Hello everyone! And welcome to TOP 10 FACTS ABOUT MAGNUS CARLSEN

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.260
Number 1

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.780
In February 2015. Carlsen broke Garry Kasparov’s record

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.740
by clocking the highest Elo rating of all time—2,872

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:17.800
In 2009, at the age of 19, he became the youngest world No.1, breaking the record held by Kramnik.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.060
Number 2

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:23.400
When Carlsen trains for a big event, like the upcoming world championships,

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.360
it usually involves spending two to three weeks in a place with good weather and the sea.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:31.520
He and his team of advisers and trainers spend most of the day working on chess,

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.340
but also go for long swims, and play basketball and football.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:35.840
Number 3

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.780
Carlsen does not watch many movies

00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:42.300
because he does not have the patience to sit through one-and-a-half or 2 hours of screen time, he says.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.520
Instead, he unwinds by watching TV serials. His favourite is Seinfeld, which he has seen multiple times.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:48.760
Number 4

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:52.720
When Carlsen was 12, his parents took him and his two sisters out of school for a year,

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:57.240
sold their car, put their house on rent, and took the entire family on a year-long round-the-world holiday

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.440
which combined chess workshops and chess tournaments.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:06.360
That year off school meant that Carlsen never really found a taste for institutionalized education, and did not go to university.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:11.320
Towards the end of that year, Carlsen was paired up to play against Kasparov in a speed chess tournament.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.760
Carlsen played the Russian legend to a draw. He celebrated by eating ice cream at McDonald’s.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:19.680
In 2009, five years after that first meeting, Kasparov became his coach.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.560
Number 5

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:26.400
A football and basketball fan, Carlsen is also perhaps the only chess player who has bagged modelling assignments.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:33.760
He appeared alongside actor Liv Tyler for the Dutch designer label G-Star Raw’s 2010 campaign, and continues to be their brand ambassador.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.360
Number 6

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.560
At 2 years of age, he could solve 50-piece jigsaw puzzle.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.360
Number 7

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:44.560
He blindfolded beat 10 Harward lawyers simultaneously at chess.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:45.680
Number 8

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.120
Magnus Carlsen is not just one of  the best chess players on the planet,

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:51.320
he's also been voted one of the sexiest men alive.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:56.880
The UK edition of the women's magazine Cosmopolitan published a list of the "Sexiest Men of 2013"

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.160
and amongst the actors, singers and assorted other celebrities is the world's #1 ranked chess player.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.400
The magazine described Carlsen as a "hottie".

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:06.400
Number 9

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.240
Carlsen says that if he gets bored by chess, he will try something else.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.160
For me, it’s about playing as long as I’m motivated, as long as it’s fun, as long as it’s interesting.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:19.480
And as long as that happens, I’m going to continue playing. Whether that’s till I’m 30 , till I’m 40, or 50 going

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:22.080
Carlsen said in an interview with Business insider.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:26.800
If I quit, I would probably start by studying something that interests me. But I don’t know what ...

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:31.200
Maybe if I didn’t have the talent for chess, I’d find the talent in something else, he said.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.680
And NUMBER 10

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.280
Magnus is a big Fischer fan.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.280
He said for the interview for CNN:

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:39.040
If I could choose my opponent to be anyone in chess history,

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.360
It would probably be Bobby Fischer at his best.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.360
Because the precision and energy that he played with

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.360
is just unmatched in the history of chess.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.440
So, Bobby Fischer from 1970 to 1972.

